lib/segment/src/index/struct_payload_index/read_view/filtering.rs:104-110

Condition::IsEmpty(IsEmptyCondition { is_empty: field }) => {
    let available_points = self.available_point_count();
    let condition = FieldCondition::new_is_empty(field.key.clone(), true);

    self.estimate_field_condition(&condition, nested_path, hw_counter)?
        .unwrap_or_else(|| CardinalityEstimation::unknown(available_points))
}

This code shows that IsEmpty conditions delegate to field index cardinality estimation. For keyword indexes, the estimation appears to use a coarse heuristic (likely falling back to unknown() or an imprecise index-based estimate), resulting in systematic under-counting. The exact path scans all points and returns 4, while the approximate indexed path returns only 2 (50% error), exceeding the 20% tolerance threshold defined in the cardinality_oracle bug shape.
